From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathieu GRENET <mathieu@mgth.fr>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:36:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 47/50] ad_iamf_iec61937: keep the restart marker in its
 decoder

The marker saying that a (re)start has not reached the audio output yet
was a static of the process. Several mpv_create() instances can run in
one process, each with its own decoder and output: one cleared another's
pending restart, and one's seek made another open its sequence again
(re-review of mgth/mpv#32: of 16 concurrent instances, 15 did not have
exactly one opening burst).

The marker is now the decoder's own. The player reports a burst it is
about to send to the decoder that made it, through its track's decoder
wrapper (ADCTRL_IAMF_BURST_SENT), which opens the sequence on it if a
restart is pending. Only bursts that lead with a copy of the descriptors
are reported: a few after a restart, then one per copy interval, so the
wrapper's lock is not taken per frame.

Checked: 16 libmpv instances in one process, separate PCM outputs,
--start=2.5 and no copy interval, each open on their first burst and
only there. The single-player cases are unchanged (start, seek at start,
seeks during playback, also with the decoder on its own thread), and the
output from the start is still byte-identical to `orender
wrap-iec61937`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
